Sometimes you may want to temporarily remove a beat from public view without permanently deleting it. That’s where the Archive feature comes in handy. Archiving a beat means it's hidden from the marketplace, but you can still access it privately from your dashboard and restore it anytime.

### How to Archive Your Beat on Beat22:

1.  **Go to Your Dashboard** Log into your Beat22 seller account and head over to your dashboard.
2.  ****Click on Browse at the top****
    
    ![Click on Browse at the top](/images/2025/06/Screenshot-2025-06-30-210101.png)
    
3.  ****Click on “My Beats”****
    
    ![Click on “My Beats”](/images/2025/06/Screenshot-2025-07-01-001344.png)
    
4.  ****Click on the “Active” Button****
    
    ![Click on the “Active” Button](/images/2025/06/Screenshot-2025-07-01-001400.png)
    
5.  ****A pop-up will appear, select “Yes” to confirm. Your beat will be archived.****
    
    ![A pop-up will appear, select “Yes” to confirm. Your beat will be archived.](/images/2025/06/Screenshot-2025-07-01-001412.png)
